      "case": "English keeps April commercial rebate separate from data authorization",
      "language": "en",
      "pass": true,
      "answer": "\n\nFive percent, and no. As of 21 April the April Atlas invoice carries the 5% rebate, because the binding document is still Renewal Agreement v2.0, countersigned by Malik Ahmed on 26 February for the 2026 contract year, and Priya confirmed the same in writing on 21 April. Appendix v2.1 from 6 April is still pending signature, its rebate rate is not even fixed in the draft, and it only takes effect for periods commencing 1 May once fully executed, so nothing else may be applied to April. For context, the 4% figure is historical: it was the 2025 rate, and the January invoice INV-2026-02-001 was processed at 4% and will not be adjusted.\n\nThe commercial position does not unlock the migration. That is gated by a separate blocker, clause 3 of the v2.1 draft: production data exchange stays blocked until DPA-42 v3.0 is countersigned by Atlas legal. Lucía's handoff note on the v1.2 test batch says the same, staging mapping is fine but the production load cannot run, and the security audit matter is still sitting in waiting status with the next step being to hold data movement until the signed DPA arrives. So the two tracks are independent: invoice at 5% now, chase the DPA-42 countersignature for the cutover.",
